draft_notes.limitations:
- d4 is accepted but unused, because the rule is D4-equivariant once mirror orientation is read from the pixels.
- Bent or diagonal red components are skipped. The constructor never produces them.
- The program relies on the constructor's invariants:
  - each shape touches exactly one mirror;
  - distinct shapes and distinct mirrors are not 8-adjacent;
  - the background is the strict majority colour;
  - reflections of different colours never collide.
- Demonstrations are not consulted.
- I found no fixture contradictions or constructor defects.
